    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7086\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Lewisboro in the county\nof Westchester, to discontinue the use of certain park land and lease\nsuch land for use of a wireless communications facility\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nAuthorizes the town of Lewisboro to discontinue use of certain park\nland and lease such land for use of a wireless communications\nfacility.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1: Authorizes the town of Lewisboro to discontinue the use of\ncertain park land and to sell and convey the land which is no longer\nneeded for park purposes at fair market value to New York SMSA limited\npartnership, d/b/a Verizon Wireless.\n\nSection 2: Describes the parks lands to be leased by the town of\nLewisboro.\n\nSection 3: States that this act· shall take effect only upon the\ncondition that the town of Lewisboro substitute and designate as park\nlands, land of equivalent fair market value and recreational\nusefulness to the lands being alienated.\n\nSection 4: Describes the park lands to be substituted by the town of\nLewisboro.\n\nSection 5: States the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation was requested by the Town of Lewisboro.  The property\nto be alienated is a 2.76 acre portion of the parcel located at 1065\nRoute 35, and designated as Sheet 21, Block 10541, Lot 25 in the Town\nof Lewisboro, Westchester County. The Town proposes to replace the\nparcel with a 3.0 acre parcel of property owned by the town.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
