    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7086B\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Lewisboro in the county\nof Westchester, to discontinue the use of certain park land and lease\nsuch land for use of a wireless communications facility\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nAuthorizes the town of Lewisboro to discontinue use of certain park\nland and lease such land for use of a wireless communications\nfacility.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1: Authorizes the town of Lewisboro to discontinue the use of\ncertain park land which is no longer needed for park purposes and\nlease the lands described in this act at fair market value to New York\nSMSA limited partnership, d/b/a Verizon Wireless, and states that all\nproceeds from such lease shall be used for the acquisition of\nadditional park lands and/or for capital improvements to existing\nparks and recreation facilities.\n\nSection 2: Describes the parks lands to be leased by the town of\nLewisboro.\n\nSection 3: Describes easements to the parkland referred to in section\none of this act which may be granted to New York SMSA limited\npartnership, d/b/a Verizon Wireless, for the purposes of installation\nof utility lines and for ingress and egress.\n\nSection 4: States that should the lands leased described in section\ntwo cease to be used for the purposes described in section one, the\nlease shall terminate and those lands shall revert to the town of\nLewisboro for public park and recreational purposes, and at the time\nof such reversion, the removal of such wireless communications\nfacility shall take place.\n\nSection 5: Describes the park lands to be substituted by the town of\nLewisboro.\n\nSection 6: States the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation was requested by the Town of Lewisboro.  The property\nto be alienated is a 2.76 acre portion of the parcel located at 1065\nRoute 35, and designated as Sheet 21, Block 10541, Lot 25 in the Town\nof Lewisboro, Westchester County.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
