    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7086C\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Lewisboro in the county of\nWestchester, to discontinue the use of certain park land\n\nPURPOSE:\nAuthorizes the town Lewisboro to discontinue use of certain park land\nand lease such land for use of a wireless communications facility.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1: Authorizes the town of Lewisboro to discontinue the use of\ncertain park land which is no longer needed for park purposes and lease\nthe lands described in this act at fair market value to New York SMSA\nlimited partnership, d/b/a Verizon Wireless.\n\nSection 2: States the authorization provided in section one of this act\nshall be effective only upon the condition that the town of Lewisboro\ndedicate an amount equal to or greater than the fair market value of the\nparkland being permanently discontinued in section three of this act and\nthe interest being alienated in sections four of this act for the acqui-\nsition of additional parklands and/or capital improvements to existing\npark and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 3: Describes the parks lands to be leased by the town of Lewis-\nboro.\n\nSection 4: Describes easements to the parkland referred to in section\none of this act which may be granted to New York SMSA limited partner-\nship, d/b/a Verizon Wireless, for the purposes of installation of utili-\nty lines and for ingress and egress.\n\nSection 5: States that discontinuance of parkland authorized by the\nprovisions of this act should not occur until the town of Lewisboro has\ncomplied with any federal requirements pertaining to the alienation or\nconversion of parklands.\n\nSection 6: States the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation was requested by the Town of Lewisboro.  The property\nto be alienated is a 2.76 acre portion of the parcel located at 1065\nRoute 35, and designated as Sheet 21, Block 10541, Lot 25 in the Town of\nLewisboro, Westchester County.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
